# Architecture & Shared Code

One source of truth. Apps stay thin and consume packages; packages do not import from apps.

## Monorepo Boundaries

- **One canonical source:** Shared logic, models, schemas, and crypto live in `packages/` (or `sdk/`/`core/`).
- **No cross-app imports:** Apps (`apps/*`) must never import directly from sibling apps. Common behavior belongs in a shared package.
- **Thin app rule:** App services handle orchestration and presentation only. Business logic, cryptographic signing, and storage resolvers reside in packages.
- **No plain-text secrets:** Keys, passcodes, and tokens never live in code or committed config.

## Rebuild Over Patch

- When an architecture path, shim, or abstraction is structurally broken or redundant, **delete the dead path** rather than layering shims, adapters, or fallback branches over it.
- Implement the canonical solution once in the responsible package under `packages/`.
- Trace imports and remove orphaned files, exports, and dead toggles in the same commit.

## Machine Enforcement & Ratchets

- Hard bans and architectural boundaries require automated CI/test ratchets (e.g. `scripts/check-*.sh`), not passive prose.
- Do not weaken, bypass, or expand allowlists in check scripts to make a change pass. Fix the violating import or abstraction at the root.
